# .env.example — Stack pipeline v4 environment template. Copy to `.env` and fill in; `.env` is gitignored.
#
# PRINCIPLE: secrets, personal identifiers and machine-local paths live only in env, never in committed YAML
# (thresholds, model roles, channels, plans are under configs/). Library code never auto-loads .env (nor fetchpdf's
# .env.local: stack/oa_adapter.py neutralises its import-time load). Two ways in:
#   - keys: the LLM client, the X collector and the S2/OpenAlex collectors and lookups read OPENROUTER_API_KEY,
#     OPENAI_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (direct providers), X_API_BEARER_TOKEN, SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY,
#     OPENALEX_API_KEY and the S3 store settings (below) from the environment, else from the dotenv file named by
#     STACK_ENV_FILE (D160): `STACK_ENV_FILE=.env uv run --no-sync stack build …`. The file is parsed, never sourced;
#     a variable set in the shell wins over it. v4's own code sends only these keys. STACK_MAILTO is seeded from the
#     same file at CLI start when the environment lacks it.
#   - everything else is plain process environment (export it). Do not source this file (`. ./.env`, `set -a`):
#     that exports every key to every process.

# ── Keys (read from the STACK_ENV_FILE file) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenRouter key, the env var named by configs/llm.yaml provider.api_key_env. Every call reserves against its
# run's budget first (spend in the run record). Needed by every LLM call: uncomment and fill in. SECRET.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OpenAI key, the env var named by configs/llm.yaml providers.openai.api_key_env (D714): the roles with `provider:
# openai` (extract_staged_openai, extract_main_openai; technique_staged and model_roles in plan batch-2026-10a) call
# the OpenAI API directly with it. Needed by those stages only: uncomment and fill in. SECRET.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Anthropic key, the env var named by configs/llm.yaml providers.anthropic.api_key_env: a role with `provider: anthropic`
# or a model reference `anthropic:<model id>` (D722). Sent in the x-api-key header. No production plan pins one yet;
# needed by plans that do. SECRET.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# X API bearer token for collect.x-lookup. OPTIONAL: without it the stage makes no request and its keys stay due.
# X_API_BEARER_TOKEN=
# Semantic Scholar key for collect.semantic_scholar, collect.s2-lookup and acquire's oa lane (x-api-key header; the
# lane's request gate adds it to api.semanticscholar.org requests only, D592). OPTIONAL, free; without it all three
# run on the throttled keyless pool. SECRET.
# SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY=
# OpenAlex key for collect.openalex and collect.openalex-lookup (Authorization: Bearer, never in a URL). OPTIONAL:
# without it they run keyless on the free daily budget and warn once per run. Every keyed request is reserved in the
# run's OpenAlex ledger (at most $10 a run, stack/collect/provider_keys.py), capped by its stage options max_requests /
# max_usd (default $0.50). The older name OPENALEXAPIKEY is not read. SECRET.
# OPENALEX_API_KEY=

# ── Store, plan, config, spend caps (all OPTIONAL) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLI defaults for --store (a path, or s3://<bucket>/<prefix> for an S3 store; default: v4/store-dev under the
# repository, whatever the current directory) and --plan (no default: run, fold, release, the eval verbs triage,
# screen, affiliation, model_roles, technique_roles and audit-prompts, diff with `latest` and acquire reopen need it; build takes the plan as its argument).
# STACK_STORE=s3://stack-data/stack-v4
# Where s3:// stores are mirrored: $STACK_MIRROR/<bucket>/<prefix>/ (default v4/mirror under the repository; git-ignored).
# STACK_MIRROR=/data/stack-mirror
# STACK_PLAN=configs/plans/dev-v2-m4.yaml
# The YAML registry directory (default <repo>/configs).
# STACK_CONFIG_DIR=./configs
# Operator tools' cache directory (default $XDG_STATE_HOME/stack, else ~/.local/state/stack); no run writes there.
# STACK_STATE_DIR=~/.local/state/stack
# Per-run caps that can only lower the $10 per-run limits of X (stack/collect/xapi.py) and keyed OpenAlex
# (stack/collect/provider_keys.py). Each run's spend is in its run record.
# STACK_X_CAP_USD=10
# STACK_OPENALEX_CAP_USD=10

# ── Outbound proxy (OPTIONAL, unset by default; process environment only, NOT read from this file) ─────
# The standard variables: urllib, requests (the oa lane, fetchpdf) and Chromium read them natively; nothing in stack
# reads them (D680). For a later egress-filtering proxy (docs/FUTURE.md, "Egress filtering"). Export them, e.g.:
# export HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:3128 HTTP_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:3128 NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1

# ── Politeness ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Contact address for polite API pools: acquire's oa lane (Unpaywall refuses anonymous callers), collect.openalex,
# the OpenAlex/S2 lookups, arXiv and Crossref requests. A personal identifier, so env only. Provider keys: above.
# Needed by acquire's oa lane: uncomment and put your own address (the code does not reject the placeholder).
# STACK_MAILTO=you@example.org
# v3's name, read BEFORE STACK_MAILTO by the provider Gate's pacing and the response journal (provider_transport.py):
# a stale export from v3 days wins. Leave unset.
# STACK_METADATA_MAILTO=
# fetchpdf's contact (the oa lane and the convert ladder seed it from STACK_MAILTO when unset).
# EMAIL=

# ── Collect knobs (all OPTIONAL; a plan line's `options:` sets the same, the env var WINS and never enters the config
#    digest. A cap or sampling variable (*_LIMIT, *_FRACTION, *_MAX_QUERIES) that is set makes `stack build` and
#    `stack run collect.*` refuse to start unless --allow-env-limits, which records the values as env_limits, D553:
#    leave unset for builds you keep) ─────
# Shared by the query-driven collectors: per-run cap, stable query fraction (0, 1], cap on queries swept.
# STACK_COLLECT_LIMIT=0
# STACK_COLLECT_FRACTION=1
# STACK_COLLECT_MAX_QUERIES=0
# Floors (from-dates) and full re-sweeps per channel.
# STACK_ARXIV_FROM=  STACK_OPENALEX_FROM=  STACK_S2_FROM=  STACK_FORUMS_FROM=  STACK_AF_FROM=
# STACK_OPENALEX_FULL=0  STACK_S2_FULL=0  STACK_CARDS_FULL=0
# collect.openalex: resume a failed run's window (see workflows/collect/openalex/README.md).
# STACK_OPENALEX_RETRY_FAILED_RUN=
# collect.arxiv_sweep roster (default configs/rosters/researchers.yaml); forums tags and karma floor.
# STACK_ARXIV_ROSTER=
# STACK_FORUMS_TAGS=
# STACK_FORUMS_MIN_KARMA=
# collect.cards / collect.blogs: per-run cap and named-source restriction.
# STACK_CARDS_LIMIT=0  STACK_CARDS_ONLY=  STACK_BLOGS_LIMIT=0  STACK_BLOGS_ONLY=
# collect.card-dates-lookup: cap, channels, refresh.
# STACK_CARD_DATES_LIMIT=0  STACK_CARD_DATES_CHANNELS=  STACK_CARD_DATES_REFRESH=0
# collect.x-lookup: keys per run.
# STACK_X_LIMIT=
# The OpenAlex/S2 lookups' per-run cap (0 = none); the response-journal directory of a caller without a store (no
# stage writes one; `python -m stack.evals.sr` sets it from --cache); the shared provider cooldown state.
# STACK_METADATA_LIMIT=0
# STACK_METADATA_SPOOL=~/.cache/stack/metadata-spool
# STACK_PROVIDER_STATE=~/.cache/stack/providers

# ── Acquire and convert (all OPTIONAL) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# fetchpdf's tier order and per-host limits for the oa lane (default: configs/fetchpdf_ladder.json).
# FETCHPDF_LADDER=configs/fetchpdf_ladder.json
# Skip docling in the conversion ladder ("1"); OCR on docling's primary pass ("1").
# STACK_CONVERT_NO_DOCLING=0
# STACK_DOCLING_PRIMARY_OCR=0

# ── TLS (OPTIONAL) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The CA bundle of the LLM client's transport (stack/llm/__init__.py): SSL_CERT_FILE, else AWS_CA_BUNDLE. The
# collectors' HTTP (stack/http.py): SSL_CERT_FILE, else REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE.
# REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE=
# SSL_CERT_FILE=
# AWS_CA_BUNDLE=

# ── S3 store (OPTIONAL; only for `--store s3://<bucket>/<prefix>`, D321; boto3 is in the `s3` uv group, which the
#    default `dev` group includes) ──
# The bucket and prefix come from the store URI; a bucket may hold several stores, one prefix each. Blobs, records,
# logs and data all live under that prefix (docs/howto/s3-store.md). Read from the environment, else from the
# STACK_ENV_FILE file, as explicit keys (never boto3's ambient chain). STACK_S3_DEFAULT_REGION defaults to "auto".
# The older names STACK_S3_ENDPOINT, AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, STACK_S3_REGION are still accepted;
# per setting the new name, in the environment or this file, wins over the old one in either (D726).
# SECRET: STACK_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID, STACK_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY.
# STACK_S3_ENDPOINT_URL=https://<the S3 endpoint of the provider>
# STACK_S3_DEFAULT_REGION=auto
# STACK_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# STACK_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# ── Eval-set whole texts (OPTIONAL; D790) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the frozen eval sets' whole texts are cached (not in the repository; tools/fetch_eval_texts.py fills it).
# Default: $XDG_CACHE_HOME/stack/eval-texts, else ~/.cache/stack/eval-texts.
# STACK_EVAL_TEXTS_DIR=

# ── Operator display ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "0" silences the live progress display (default: on when stderr is a TTY).
# STACK_PROGRESS=

# ── Worker threads ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A ceiling on every stage pool's threads (D786); unset = only the cgroup's task room (pids.max) less 128 caps them.
# STACK_POOL_MAX_THREADS=

# ── Dormant code paths (no v4 stage reads these) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# fetchpdf (acquire's oa lane), neutralised by stack/oa_adapter.py: its .env.local is not loaded, and its own key
# reads (OPENALEXAPIKEY, COREAPIKEY, SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY, ENTREZ_EUTILS_API_KEY, SCOPUS_API_KEY,
# ELSEVIER_TDM_API_KEY) are cleared or stripped from its requests; its OpenAlex calls stay keyless. Its S2 requests
# carry our SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY (above), added by our request gate, not by fetchpdf (D592).
# Test hooks, not for operators: STACK_LLM_TRANSPORT, STACK_WORKFLOWS_ROOT, STACK_CRASH_AT, STACK_CONVERT_{ABORT,
# HANG,REPORT}, STACK_{CARDS,BLOGS}_FIXTURES.
